*> Acceptance test of the suggestions of docs/protocol/15a-brigadier-command-library.md §6 (§9.2 S1 to
*> S9 on the tree of §9; S10, integer suggestions of a custom provider, has no provider yet) and
*> 15-commands-framework.md §14.2: the suggestion context of a parse and a cursor (§6.3), every child of
*> the context's parent asked (a literal by the lower-case prefix of what is typed, a bool for true and
*> false), the text equal to what is typed dropped, the list sorted by lower-case text. The result is
*> the common range start and length and the entries (Command Suggestions 0x0F). A case reads
*> [start,length] and the entries, "-" for none.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CMD-15A-6.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY BRIGADIER.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-CASES.
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "fo$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 2.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[0,2] foo".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "foo $".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 4.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[4,0] bar".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "foo b$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 5.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[4,1] bar".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "foo 5$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 2.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[0,2] foo".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "foo 5$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 3.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[0,0] -".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "b $".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 2.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[2,0] false true".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "b t$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 3.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[2,1] true".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "b true$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 6.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[0,0] -".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "run f$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 5.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[4,1] foo".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "FO$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 2.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[0,2] foo".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[0,0] b d each f foo name run say tp".
    05 FILLER PIC X(48) VALUE "name x$".
    05 FILLER PIC 9(4) VALUE 6.
    05 FILLER PIC X(96) VALUE "[0,0] -".
 01 WS-TABLE REDEFINES WS-CASES.
    05 WS-CASE              OCCURS 12 TIMES.
       10 WS-CASE-LINE       PIC X(48).
       10 WS-CASE-CURSOR     PIC 9(4).
       10 WS-CASE-EXPECTED   PIC X(96).
 01 WS-LINE                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 4096.
 01 WS-TRANSACTION         BINARY-LONG VALUE 7.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-START               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LEN                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STRING              PIC X(64).
 01 WS-STRING-CAPACITY     BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-STRING-LENGTH       BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FLAG                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MAX                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 32767.
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CURSOR              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LEVEL               BINARY-LONG VALUE 4.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-POS                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-E                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-NODE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CHILD               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CREATED             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(32).
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KIND                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FOO                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RUN                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-EACH                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TP                  BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     PERFORM BUILD-TREE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 12
         MOVE WS-CASE-LINE(WS-I) TO WS-LINE
         MOVE WS-CASE-CURSOR(WS-I) TO WS-CURSOR
         PERFORM CHECK
     END-PERFORM
     PERFORM CHECK-PACKET
     GOBACK.

*> Command Suggestions 0x0F for "b " (cursor 2): transaction id, start 2, length 0, false and true each
*> without a tooltip.
 CHECK-PACKET.
     MOVE "b $" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 2 TO WS-CURSOR
     MOVE 2 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE SPACE TO WS-LINE(3:1)
     CALL "BR-SUGGEST" USING WS-LEVEL WS-LINE WS-LENGTH WS-CURSOR
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "BR-SUGGESTIONS-BUILD" USING WS-TRANSACTION PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ID
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TX
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-START
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-LEN
     CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-N
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-POS
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     MOVE WS-TX TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     MOVE WS-START TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     MOVE WS-LEN TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     MOVE WS-N TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-E FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-E > WS-N
         CALL "PB-GET-STRING" USING PB-BUFFER WS-MAX WS-STRING WS-STRING-CAPACITY WS-STRING-LENGTH
         CALL "PB-GET-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-FLAG
         MOVE WS-FLAG TO WS-EDIT
         STRING " " WS-STRING(1:WS-STRING-LENGTH) "/" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE
             INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15a§6 Suggestions the Command Suggestions packet of [b ] reads transaction,"
         & " range and entries" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "15 7 2 0 2 false/0 true/0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

 ADD-NODE.
*> parent in WS-NODE, WS-KIND, WS-NAME (trimmed), WS-TYPE: the child id in WS-CHILD.
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-NAME)) TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "BR-ADD-NODE" USING WS-NODE WS-KIND WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-TYPE WS-CHILD WS-CREATED.

 LITERAL-NODE.
     MOVE BR-LITERAL TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 0 TO WS-TYPE
     PERFORM ADD-NODE.

 ARGUMENT-NODE.
     MOVE BR-ARGUMENT TO WS-KIND
     PERFORM ADD-NODE.

 BUILD-TREE.
     CALL "BR-TREE-RESET"
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "foo" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-FOO
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-FOO)
     MOVE WS-FOO TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "n" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE BR-P-INTEGER TO WS-TYPE
     PERFORM ARGUMENT-NODE
     MOVE 2 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-HAS-MAX(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-HAS-MIN(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-IMIN(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 10 TO BR-N-IMAX(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE "bar" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE 3 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "say" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "msg" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE BR-P-STRING TO WS-TYPE
     PERFORM ARGUMENT-NODE
     MOVE 4 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE BR-S-GREEDY TO BR-N-STRING-KIND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "tp" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-TP
     MOVE WS-TP TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "x" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE BR-P-INTEGER TO WS-TYPE
     PERFORM ARGUMENT-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "y" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM ARGUMENT-NODE
     MOVE 5 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "name" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "s" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE BR-P-STRING TO WS-TYPE
     PERFORM ARGUMENT-NODE
     MOVE 6 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE BR-S-PHRASE TO BR-N-STRING-KIND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "d" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "v" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE BR-P-DOUBLE TO WS-TYPE
     PERFORM ARGUMENT-NODE
     MOVE 7 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "f" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "v" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE BR-P-FLOAT TO WS-TYPE
     PERFORM ARGUMENT-NODE
     MOVE 8 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-HAS-MIN(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-HAS-MAX(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 0 TO BR-N-DMIN(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-DMAX(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "b" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "flag" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE BR-P-BOOL TO WS-TYPE
     PERFORM ARGUMENT-NODE
     MOVE 9 TO BR-N-COMMAND(WS-CHILD)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NODE
     MOVE "run" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-RUN
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-REDIRECT(WS-RUN)
     MOVE "each" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM LITERAL-NODE
     MOVE WS-CHILD TO WS-EACH
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-REDIRECT(WS-EACH)
     MOVE 1 TO BR-N-FORK(WS-EACH).


 CHECK.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LENGTH
     INSPECT WS-LINE TALLYING WS-LENGTH FOR CHARACTERS BEFORE INITIAL "$"
     MOVE SPACE TO WS-LINE(WS-LENGTH + 1:1)
     CALL "BR-SUGGEST" USING WS-LEVEL WS-LINE WS-LENGTH WS-CURSOR
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-POS
     MOVE BR-SG-START TO WS-EDIT
     STRING "[" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "," DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     MOVE BR-SG-LENGTH TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "]" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     IF BR-SG-COUNT = 0
         STRING " -" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     END-IF
     PERFORM VARYING WS-E FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-E > BR-SG-COUNT
         STRING " " BR-SG-TEXT(WS-E)(1:BR-SG-TEXT-LENGTH(WS-E)) DELIMITED BY SIZE
             INTO WS-TEXT WITH POINTER WS-POS
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-CURSOR TO WS-EDIT
     STRING "acceptance US13 15a§6 Suggestions [" WS-LINE(1:WS-LENGTH) "] cursor " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-CASE-EXPECTED(WS-I) TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM TEST-CMD-15A-6.
